---
title: Hot cumin lamb wrap with crunchy slaw & spicy mayo
description: A healthy kebab flatbread - make double the cabbage and carrot coleslaw and have leftovers for lunch
time required: 18 minutes
cook time: 8 minutes
servings: 4
prep time: 10 minutes
course: Dinner, Main course
cuisine: Middle Eastern
author: Good Food team
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/hot-cumin-lamb-wrap-crunchy-slaw-spicy-mayo
---

-- Note: The image is from a converted recipe on TheMealDB using ground lamb meat, while the original BBC recipe uses a sliced leg of lamb.

> The Peppadew peppers are round red piquante peppers sold in jars.

Heat a #griddle pan{} or #large skillet{} over medium-high heat.

Rub the @lamb leg steaks{4%small} with the @olive oil{2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%heaped tsp}, and some @salt{} and @pepper{}.
Cook for about ~{3-4%minutes} on each side or until cooked to your liking. Place to one side on a plate to rest.

In a large bowl, stir the @sugar{1%tbsp} into the @white wine vinegar{3%tbsp} until dissolved.
Add the @carrots{2}(coarsely grated), @spring onions{2}(finely sliced),
@white cabbage{8%oz}(very finely sliced), and some @salt{} and @pepper{}, and toss together.

Blend the @sweet peppadew peppers{5}(whole) with @mayonnaise{3%tbsp} to create a sandwich spread.

Add a heap of the vegetable mix to each @pita{4}(or flatbread, warmed). 
Slice the lamb, trimming off any excess fat, and lay on top of the salad, drizzling with the resting juices.
Spoon over the mayo and scatter with a extra @sweet peppadew peppers{2}(roughly sliced).

Roll up and eat. If using pitta, split and stuff. Serve any extra salad on the side.

= Nutritional Info (per serving) =
661 calories; 29g fat; 7g saturated fat; 67g carbohydrates; 21g sugar; 30g protein; 9g fiber; 1.5mg sodium
